id: internal-attack
name: Internal Attack
type: standard
actionCost: 2
kiCostPerTier: 6
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
clashSaves: impulsive
clashDefenderSaves: impulsive, corporeal
internalAttack: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Get inside them. Win the Clash and you leave the Encounter while they lose 2(T) of
  Soak Value and Defense Value - and you come back out where you like, for twice your
  Might straight off their Life Points.
text: >
  Internal Attack Maneuver [1/Round]: You are able to enter a target’s body and attack
  them from within!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 2 Actions
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –KP Cost: 6(T)
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent within your Melee Range. Make a Clash (Impulsive vs
  Impulsive/Corporeal) against them. If you win, remove yourself from the Combat Encounter
  (record your Initiative) and while you are not a member of the Combat Encounter, reduce
  their Soak Value and Defense Value by 2(T). As an Instant Maneuver, despite not being
  involved in the Combat Encounter, you can appear on a Square adjacent to the target of
  this Maneuver, re-enter the Combat Encounter (using your recorded Initiative), and
  reduce their Life Points by 2x your Might.

---

# --- The Clash ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "(Impulsive vs Impulsive/Corporeal)" - the first Saving Throw Clash in these rules with a
# different throw on each side. One named for the challenger and two for the defender, and
# that slash is a choice the defender makes, the same slash as in "Strike/Dodge".
#
# The Thrust's "(Impulsive/Corporeal)" has no `vs` in it and stays what it was: one list
# offered to both sides.
#
# A tie goes to the Defender, here as everywhere.
#
# --- Being inside somebody ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two halves, and only one of them is this system's to do.
#
# "Remove yourself from the Combat Encounter (record your Initiative)" is a change to the
# Initiative Order, and this system does not add or remove combatants - the Order is the
# ARC's, and taking somebody out of it mid-round is exactly the sort of thing that should
# happen where everyone can see it. So the Initiative is recorded, the card says it, and
# whoever runs the tracker does the rest.
#
# What IS done is the state itself: the attacker is marked as being inside somebody, and
# the target is marked as having somebody inside them. That pair is what "while you are not
# a member of the Combat Encounter" comes to at this table - it begins when the Clash is
# won and ends when you burst out - and it is what carries the penalty.
#
# The penalty lives in the mark's own file, which is where a reader looks for what being
# Internalized costs.
#
# --- Coming back out ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "As an Instant Maneuver... you can appear on a Square adjacent to the target, re-enter the
# Combat Encounter (using your recorded Initiative), and reduce their Life Points by 2x your
# Might."
#
# An Instant, so it releases the Instant rule and cannot follow another Instant, and the
# card is where it is taken from - the button is on the Clash that put you in there, and it
# belongs to the one who is inside.
#
# The Might is read when you come out rather than when you went in: it is "your Might",
# present tense, and a Power Up while you were inside is yours.
#
# A Life Point reduction, which in these rules means straight off their Life Points past
# the Soak Value and the Damage Reduction - the same thing a collision is, and it goes
# through the same function.
#
# Where you appear is the table's, like every Square in this system.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Minions: Non-Minion" - the first entry to name that restriction rather than Free or N/A,
# and there are no Minions here to refuse. Carried as printed.
#
# Nothing stops a second character getting inside the same target, and nothing stops you
# acting while you are in there beyond the Order not reaching you - both of which follow
# from the Encounter membership being the table's.
#
# --- How it is gained -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Special Maneuver, and what opens it has not been read yet.
